+\subsection{Reconstruction and Measured Cost}
+\label{subsec:revision-research-verification}
+
+Separate replay drivers regenerate the native-gradient queries and selected
+aggregates, reproduce all seven terminal numerical failures, and repeat the
+relevant local training. A complete second execution of the common-input
+comparison reproduces all 840 outputs and 1,801 numerical files byte for
+byte. The group driver repeats the selections, all 106 direct outputs and
+all 23 continuation branches, including 115 future aggregates. These are
+checks using the same numerical implementation, not independent external
+validation. They supplement the formal hypotheses rather than proving them.
